is predictable, so that   G 3   is unfavorable to her As shown in Table V, DQN and PPO achieve a higher win rate compared with that in the symmetric case   G 0 This again demonstrates DQN and PPO can take advantage of the asymmetric structure of the graph These three cases demonstrate that both DQN and PPO can effectively leverage the structural advantages of the graph to improve their win rates Conversely, in all the scenarios above where the structure of the graph inherently puts Player 2 at a disadvantage, we'::text, 'doc'::varchar(50), NULL, '{}'::jsonb, ''0':33,87,165 '1':8,110 '2':26,70,94,117,122,127,220 '22':82 '3':72,81,85,97,124,139 '33':86 '4':68 '71':58 '86':51 'achiev':49,56,152 'action':129 'addit':112 'advantag':42,174,196 'asymmetr':23,177 'better':21 'cannot':73 'case':163,184 'clear':3 'com':27 'compar':157 'continu':4 'convers':205 'demonstr':14,168,185 'disadvantag':223 'distribut':1,115 'dqn':16,37,48,149,169,188 'effect':192 'experiment':9 'favor':6 'first':132 'g':25,32,67,80,84,138,164 'graph':24,31,45,181,199,216 'h':79,83 'higher':154 'ical':78 'improv':201 'indic':35 'inher':217 'leverag':193 'mean':89 'must':102 'node':69,93,96,107,121 'pare':28 'perform':19 'player':7,116,126,219 'ppo':18,39,55,151,171,190 'predict':135 'present':62 'put':218 'random':114 'rate':53,60,156,204 'realloc':104 'resourc':76,91,119 'result':10 'retain':74 'scenario':209 'setup':2 'shown':145 'signific':20 'specif':47,77 'step':100,133 'structur':46,178,195,213 'symmetr':30,162 'tabl':12,64,147 'take':41,173 'therefor':125 'three':183 'time':99 'unfavor':141 'v':13,65,148 'win':52,59,155,203'::tsvector, NOW()),
