ts to reflect varying levels of strategic importance   across   the   graph This   extension   will   require adapting our model to account for weighted nodes, and we aim to investigate whether RL methods can effectively optimize strategies under these conditions Third, while resources are currently allocated in discrete units, we aim to extend our framework to handle scenarios where resources are treated as continuous variables Finally, we aim to address the case of heterogeneous resources, where each player controls multiple resource types that exhibit mutual counteractions [17] This setting introduces additional strategic complexity, and we will'::text, 'doc'::varchar(50), NULL, '{}'::jsonb, ''17':187 '34':66 '35':70 '36':75 '37':82 'account':122 'across':86,111 'adapt':118 'addit':191 'address':170 'advantag':31 'agent':90 'aim':128,151,168 'al':59 'algorithm':62 'alloc':146 'base':50 'case':172 'compar':17 'complex':193 'condit':140 'conduct':84 'constraint':1 'continu':164 'control':179 'counteract':186 'current':145 'ddpg':81 'deep':77 'demonstr':22 'determinist':78 'disadvantag':4,40 'discret':148 'divers':87 'doubl':64 'dqn':26,65,69 'du':67 'effect':28,135 'ele':68 'enhanc':8 'evalu':58 'exhibit':184 'experi':72,85 'exploit':29 'explor':44 'extend':153 'extens':46,115 'final':166 'first':54 'framework':51,155 'futur':41 'gradient':80 'grag':53 'graph':113 'handl':157 'heterogen':174 'higher':14 'import':110 'includ':63 'intend':97 'introduc':99,190 'investig':130 'learn':92 'level':107 'marl':93 'method':133 'mitig':33 'model':120 'multi':89 'multi-ag':88 'multipl':180 'mutual':185 'node':101,125 'node-specif':100 'optim':136 'per':74 'perform':10 'plan':56 'player':178 'polici':79 'ppo':24 'priorit':71 'rate':16 'reflect':105 'reinforc':91 'relat':39 'replay':73 'requir':117 'research':42 'resourc':3,38,143,160,175,181 'resource-rel':37 'result':11 'rl':5,49,61,132 'scenario':158 'second':95 'set':189 'sever':45 'simul':94 'specif':102 'still':7 'strateg'