ion terms are designed to either help policy randomization and exploration Mutti et al (2021; 2022), or to stabilize RL algorithms However, these  2 See the project repository https://github.com/tud-amr/parl for details 2'::text, 'doc'::varchar(50), NULL, '{}'::jsonb, ''/tud-amr/parl':140 '1.1':64 '1991':86 '2':63,133,143 '2010':94 '2013':97 '2015':90 '2017':101 '2021':124 '2022':125 '2023':105 'achiev':51 'agent':49 'al':89,93,100,104,123 'algorithm':79,130 'also':7 'autonom':60 'averag':2 'design':113 'detail':142 'drive':61 'either':115 'employ':16 'entropi':4,10,28,74 'entropy-r':27 'estim':26 'et':88,92,99,103,122 'exist':5 'explor':83,120 'extens':82 'final':40 'form':72 'fox':87 'function':31 'github.com':139 'github.com/tud-amr/parl':138 'gradient':38,78 'help':116 'howev':131 'idea':68 'incorpor':33 'instanc':108 'introduc':70 'learn':18 'minim':8 'model':19 'much':46 'mutti':121 'near':53 'near-optim':52 'neu':96,98 'object':75 'optim':54 'parl':44 'peng':85 'peter':91 'polici':37,77,117 'policy-gradi':36 'predict':48 'produc':45 'project':136 'random':118 'rate':11,29 'regular':110 'relat':65 'repositori':137 'reward':23,55 'rl':129 'robot':58 'scheme':39 'see':134 'sever':57 'show':14 'showcas':42 'stabil':128 'surrog':3,22 'task':62 'term':111 'tiapkin':102 'valu':30 'william':84 'work':66 'zimin':95'::tsvector, NOW()),
