reby yileding that deterministic local minimizers of   ¯ h π s   are also local minimizers of   ¯ h π Finally, the third statement follows as a combination of the other two Theorem 1 is an utterly relevant result for our work First, it guarantees that minimizing policies both for   ¯ h π s  and   ¯ h π   exist More importantly, it tells us that,   to minimize the entropy rate of an RL agent, it is sufficient to minimize the surrogate entropy rate Since (globally) minimizing   ¯ h π s   implies minimizing   ¯ h π   and since   s   is policy-independent, in contrast to   l π   , in what follows, our RL algorithm uses estimates of   s   to minimize   ¯ h π s   , instead of estimates of   l π   to minimize   ¯ h π 10  10 Observe that we cannot employ the same method for entropy rate maximization, since the maximizer of   ¯ h π s   is not necessarily a maximizer of   ¯ h π 6'::text, 'doc'::varchar(50), NULL, '{}'::jsonb, ''1':35,76,170 '10':265,266 '3':43 '6':294 'agent':208 'algorithm':245 'also':8,137,151 'appendix':46 'appli':138 'arg':27,114,128 'argument':136 'b':78 'c':13,80 'cannot':270 'combin':164 'contrast':236 'd':22,73,125 'determinist':1,17,55,143 'direct':40 'employ':271 'entropi':63,203,216,276 'estim':247,257 'exist':15,193 'final':157 'first':37,179 'follow':39,85,110,161,242 'global':219 'guarante':48,181 'h':5,11,30,65,91,94,97,100,106,118,132,147,155,187,191,221,226,252,263,283,292 'hold':86 'impli':224 'import':195 'independ':234 'instead':255 'l':238,259 'least':53 'lemma':75 'local':3,9,139,144,152 'maxim':278,281,290 'method':274 'min':28,115,129 'minim':4,10,60,105,145,153,183,201,213,220,225,251,262 'necessarili':288 'observ':267 'one':54 'polici':2,18,56,184,233 'policy-independ':232 'proof':32 'rate':64,204,217,277 'relev':174 'result':175 'rl':207,244 'sinc':69,218,229,279 'statement':38,77,160 'suffici':211 'surrog':62,215 'tell':197 'theorem':34,42,169 'therebi':140 'third':159 'thus':102 'two':168 'us':198 'use':246 'utter':173 'work':178 