5419326,-0.006638376,-0.009979692,-0.02954815,0.012465395,0.009212591,-0.02037244,-0.019634841,0.03720441,0.0053475806,-0.039889265,-0.0067895832,0.009898556,1.1488943e-06,0.0076636365,0.022644239,-0.021449331,0.02857452,-0.003295216,-0.006907599,0.029916948,-0.005900779,0.031362638,0.040302318,0.0114327585,0.008393858,0.016802467,-0.011683541,0.020165911,-0.03956472,-0.01095332,-0.019605337,0.023632618,0.005214813,-0.014338892,0.0075751245,0.024148937,0.023676874,-0.003051809,-0.0106214015,0.033516422,0.0022459838,-0.04298717,0.023308076,0.0076562604,0.04463939,0.010739417,0.0010630621,0.015091241,-0.010385371,0.018366173,0.036584828,-0.014906842,-0.017451553,0.017908864,-0.001638388,-0.019103771,0.005284885,-0.008873296,0.0035072754,0.029769428,-0.0004448634,0.002483859,-0.012480147,0.01280469,-0.030241491,0.029031832,0.011794182,-0.021124788,0.019207034,-0.009773165,0.010134587,-0.009065071,-0.042485606,-0.0072358297,-0.0223492,-0.0043776403,-0.0031163488,-0.0025557748,-0.009138831,-0.017466305,-0.0048718303,-0.0091019515,0.009559262,0.008858544,0.016994242,-0.022113169,-0.016566437,-0.018808732,0.0054951003,-0.015681319,0.05729656,0.016300902,0.0070883106,-0.044845916,0.020549461,-0.03227726,0.0059597865,-0.0056831874,-0.027084574,0.02857452,-0.010200971]'::vector, 'See the Appendix for these.  16 Recall that, for our implementation, to address continuous state/action tasks, we use   differential entropy   to quantify predictability for continuous random variables, which may indeed be negative.   A different metric one may use is   relative entropy   (the KL-divergence from the uniform distribution).  9

