-0.010530783,-0.0035396863,0.02045229,0.027915923,-0.03126694,0.014068739,0.0121716745,-0.004389557,-0.0014444343,-0.020853858,-0.011991661,0.0013855838,0.006951286,0.01661662,-0.014401071,-0.016021192,0.023692532,0.044504847,0.014719556,-0.0027590513,0.013701788,-0.013653323,0.01295404,-0.03220855,0.0036210385,0.020701539,0.019358363,-0.02247398,0.007027446,-0.0010117098,-0.0127671035,0.017682854,0.004244162,0.026545051,0.026171178,-0.0003055035,-0.01125776,0.014802639,-0.018209046,-0.029272946,-0.0067297313,-0.00875142,-0.005085378,-0.013909495,0.02193394,0.01725359,0.0054661757,0.0023384432,0.00929146,-0.0023990246,0.032014687,0.0053796307,0.009783035,0.0088483505,0.020743081,0.043618627,0.035171848,0.017322827,0.006411246,0.015301138,-0.0067989673,0.029439112,-0.00036716674,0.048465144,-0.012580167,0.012559395,-0.08247382,-0.015661165,0.038578253,-0.047301978,0.056274954,0.036584258,-0.056219567,-0.033565573,-0.018859863,-0.004476102,-0.011839342,-0.0049572918,-0.012940193,-0.0012886535,-0.005483485,0.009319155,0.015134972,0.007740576,0.011777029,0.014089509,-0.0034548724,-0.046886563,-0.03024225,0.021269275,0.012746332,0.024038712,0.013978732,0.00027824185,0.019012183,0.01204705,0.018056728,0.0031294634,0.012663249,0.051539216,-0.026669675]'::vector, 'In this in-depth conversation, Audit Polycha, co-founder and CEO of Zeppto, details the rapid rise and ongoing evolution of his company, which delivers groceries and other goods across India in 10 minutes, boasting over 1.5 million daily orders, $3 billion in GMV, and a $5 billion unicorn valuation. Audit emphasizes that Zeppto’s genesis was not from grand strategy but from responding directly to user needs during the pandemic, starting as a WhatsApp group delivering groceries to neighbors. This user-backward, first-principles approach—contrasting with competitors’ supply-chain-first models—enabled Zeppto to prioritize extreme speed, quality, selection, and price, resulting in higher retention and superior unit economics compared to legacy 2- or 4-hour delivery models.

Audit recounts existential crises, such as early retention problems, intense capital constraints during market downturns, and fierce competition from well-capitalized rivals. He credits Zeppto’s survival and success to radical candor, relentless iteration, and the willingness to do unscalable things—like personally running stores and making deliveries—to deeply understand customer needs and validate product-market fit. This led to innovations such as the dark store model, enabling full-stack control over logistics, improved customer experience, and expansion into a hyper-local “everything store” offering tens of thousands of products beyond groceries.

He discusses the company’s breakneck scaling, from zero to $200 million run-rate in six months and then to a billion in GMV within two and a half years, attributing this to product-market fit, disciplined capital efficiency, and a culture of executional excellence. Audit highlights the critical importance and occasional missteps in talent acquisition and management, especially during periods when survival depended on operational excellence. He notes the unique advantages of India, such as a deep and underappreciated talent pool, and the challenges of fostering a more ambitious, risk-taking mindset within the ecosystem.

Looking forward, Zeppto’s vision is to continually deepen product-market fit through relentless innovation rather than spreading thin across unrelated verticals. Recent expansions include Zeppto Cafe (first-party food delivery), a rapidly growing advertising business, and forays into new categories like electronics and cosmetics—all driven by direct user demand and data. Audit also discusses leveraging AI and machine learning to accelerate core functions such as search, ads, customer support, and supply chain forecasting, building proprietary capabilities for mission-critical applications while waiting for commoditized solutions in non-core areas.

Throughout, Audit stresses that Zeppto’s journey is far from complete, viewing it as a multi-decade endeavor to build a world-class internet company that can stand alongside global giants like Amazon and Mercado Libre. He underscores the importance of intrinsic motivation, advocating for building “for the love of building,” and fostering a culture that attracts ambitious, execution-focused talent eager to tackle meaningful challenges. Ultimately, Zeppto’s story is characterized by audacious vision, customer obsession, adaptability in the face of adversity, and an enduring commitment to create transformative value for India’s digital economy.'::text, 'summary'::varchar(50), NULL, '{}'::jsonb, ''1.5':39 '10':35 '2':120 '200':233 '3':43 '4':122 '5':49 'acceler':386 'acquisit':280 'across':32,342 'ad':392 'adapt':497 'advantag':296 'advers':502 'advertis':358 'advoc':462 'ai':381 'alongsid':447 'also':378 'amazon':451 'ambiti':314,476 'applic':406 'approach':90 'area':416 'attract':475 'attribut':254 'audaci':493 'audit':7,53,126,270,377,418 'backward':86 'beyond':221 'billion':44,50,245 'boast':37 'breakneck':228 'build':399,437,464,469 'busi':359 'cafe':349 'candor':158 'capabl':401 'capit':136,147,262 'categori':364 'ceo':13 'chain':96,397 'challeng':309,485 'character':491 'class':441 'co':10 'co-found':9 'commit':506 'commodit':410 'compani':25,226,443 'compar':117 'competit':143 'competitor':93 'complet':427 'constraint':137 'continu':329 'contrast':91 'control':200 'convers':6 'core':387,415 'cosmet':368 'creat':508 'credit':150 'crise':129 'critic':273,405 'cultur':266,473 'custom':178,204,393,495 'daili':41 'dark':193 'data':376 'decad':434 'deep':302 'deepen':330 'deepli':176 'deliv':27,79 'deliveri':124,174,354 'demand':374 'depend':288 'depth':5 'detail':16 'digit':514 'direct':67,372 'disciplin':261 'discuss':224,379 'downturn':140 'driven':370 'eager':481 'earli':132 'econom':116 'economi':515 'ecosystem':321 'effici':263 'electron':366 'emphas':54 'enabl'